      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1297197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T16:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this be `0`? Otherwise, the fan will never turn off completely, even if a duty cycle of `1` isn\u0027t enough to actually get it to spin, it seems we\u0027d still be sending it some amount of (wasted) energy.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "883203a5_36b7a482",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T16:31:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it\u0027s getting stopped here in the shim, with this delightful comment: \n```\nvoid fan_set_rpm_target(int ch, int rpm)\n{\n        if (rpm \u003d\u003d 0) {\n                /* If rpm \u003d 0, disable PWM immediately. Why?*/\n                fan_set_duty(ch, 0);\n        } else {\n\n```\n\nOne might wonder if this contributes to the abrupt on/off cycles...",
      "parentUuid": "716c3304_5bc4b813",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b696505d_f7dffc97",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1565377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T16:33:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve copied this over from https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/fan.c;l\u003d169.\n\nFrom what I can see in the EC console the fan must be turned off from another place - when the RPM is set to 0 I can see that the fan duty is also 0 using the `faninfo` EC command.",
      "parentUuid": "716c3304_5bc4b813",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95581588_cf845846",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
