      "author": {
        "id": 1565377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T16:34:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh right, thanks for finding this Diana.",
      "parentUuid": "b696505d_f7dffc97",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bdde93b_ba139e12",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1565377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T16:41:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`One might wonder if this contributes to the abrupt on/off cycles...`\n\nFrom what I can see the on/off cycles are caused by something else.\nWinterhold uses the \"linear\" approach to set the fan RPM.\nBecause of that if the temperature fluctuates at around temp_fan_off point the fan will be turned off and on repeatedly.\nThis is somewhat mitigated by setting fan rpm_min to a low value.",
      "parentUuid": "95581588_cf845846",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a252e59_93fca58e",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1297197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T17:19:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I only see `fan_set_rpm_target()` being called for markarth/frostflow:\n\n```\ntimvp@timvp-p620-9115096:~/code/cros_1/src/platform/ec/zephyr$ rg fan_set_rpm_target\nprogram/skyrim/frostflow/src/thermal.c\n107:\t\tfan_set_rpm_target(fan, fan_table_to_rpm(fan, temp));\n\nprogram/skyrim/markarth/src/thermal.c\n97:\t\tfan_set_rpm_target(fan, fan_table_to_rpm(fan, temp));\n\nprogram/nissa/yavilla/src/thermal.c\n106:\t\tfan_set_rpm_target(fan, fan_table_to_rpm(fan, temp));\n\nprogram/nissa/yaviks/src/thermal.c\n106:\t\tfan_set_rpm_target(fan, fan_table_to_rpm(fan, temp));\n\nprogram/nissa/craask/src/thermal.c\n117:\t\tfan_set_rpm_target(fan, fan_table_to_rpm(fan, temp));\n121:\t\tfan_set_rpm_target(fan, 0);\n\nshim/src/fan.c\n401:void fan_set_rpm_target(int ch, int rpm)\n```\n\nHow do we get there for winterhold?\n\nIs there a reason to keep it `1` (and hoping someone sets it to `0` somewhere else), rather than just setting it to `0` here?",
      "parentUuid": "8bdde93b_ba139e12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78aa0103_429cc2d4",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1565377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T17:24:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Winterhold uses the \"linear\" approach.\nWith that the RPM calculations are done in src/thermal.c, function thermal_control.\nMarkath/frostflow use \"fan levels\", which is implemented through board override, hence they call fan_set_rpm_target directly.\n\nSo in the case of Winterhold we have thermal_control -\u003e fan_set_percent_needed -\u003e fan_set_rpm_target.",
      "parentUuid": "4a252e59_93fca58e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb8bf854_5b9ba62b",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T17:25:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How do we get there for winterhold?\n\nI\u0027m fairly certain the path is from `fan_set_percent_needed()` in common/fan.c which is called from `thermal_control()` in common/thermal.c\n\n\u003e Winterhold uses the \"linear\" approach to set the fan RPM.\n\nI was thinking that, depending on the calls to fan_set_rpm_target(), we could potentially see a drop in duty from some non-zero number to 0 without any steps in between based on the calls into the API.  But this is an item I imagine the PID design would help with",
      "parentUuid": "8bdde93b_ba139e12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fe7fe93ca71038023e432e8aef51d52e11464624",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
